+          "at": "2026-10-19T18:55:34.010Z",
+          "author": "agent",
+          "text": "Dug in. Root cause is in our replay keying, not in copilot or GitHub.\n\nCopilot makes three POSTs to GitHub's remote MCP server at /mcp/readonly: initialize (id 0), notifications/initialized, tools/list (id 1). On replay the JSON-RPC ids and progress tokens differ, so the exact key misses. The fallback \"loose\" key is {method, path, model, last user text}, and an MCP request has neither a model nor user text, so all three POSTs share one loose key. The first stored cassette wins, and tools/list gets the wrong answer. Copilot then sees 0 MCP tools instead of 6, so its model request carries 19 tools instead of 25 ($.tools.19-24 only in the recording), and every /v1/messages call misses (rc 1 after 5 retries, 151 s).\n\nFix: when a body is JSON-RPC, put its method in the loose key, and drop id and params._meta.progressToken when normalizing. Then tools/list replays tools/list, the tool list stays 25, and the model request should key EXACT. Dispatching that now as its own piece (pr/21) on toolpath wip: a unit test for the collision, then a re-run of the copilot replay cell (no network, fake credentials) to show EXACT before claiming it."
