+          "text": "What it means: this one is staged too, like the break slide. Cassettes are recorded API exchanges we commit, so a real credential could end up in git (it nearly did: the first gemini recording wrote your real key). The no_secrets test scans every committed fixture with the rules in .gitleaks.toml, and the same file drives the gitleaks gate in CI and home's pre-commit hook (#416). The demo plants a fake sk-ant key, the test fails naming file:line and the rule, then it is reverted. v12 says that on the slide.\n\nTruffleHog: yes as an addition, not a replacement. gitleaks stays the gate, because it is offline, deterministic, and its one rules file is shared by cargo test, CI and the hook. TruffleHog (3.97.9 in nixpkgs) adds many more detectors and can verify a hit by calling the provider. Verification means sending the found secret over the network, so it does not belong in cargo test or CI on fixtures. Where it fits: home's pre-push hook, running trufflehog git file://. --since-commit <upstream> --results=verified,unknown --fail, so a live key is caught before it leaves the machine; plus a one-off full-history scan of toolpath and pathbase. Want me to add that to the home hook as its own PR?"
